  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run, using 1 of the 6 allowed runs. All 5 witnesses got their planned verdicts and the rule composes no other rule.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484D_165_3.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must belong to the vehicle aggregate defined in NRS 484A.320.\n- **When it applies:** all three of these hold.\n  - **At rest:** the vehicle is at rest, using the `drv.motion.complete_halt` concept with the `p.halt_speed_tolerance` parameter.\n  - **Where:** it occupies a roadway, or a shoulder that lies on the same highway as a roadway.\n  - **Light:** it is dark, or visibility is below 1,000 ft. Spans t4 and t6 map to the same atoms and the same figure, so I wrote this condition once rather than twice.\n- **What it requires:** the vehicle's position lamps are lit.\n- I declared no narrowings, because every span is written as the node maps it.\n\n**The witnesses:** each scene has a highway with a roadway and a paved shoulder on it, and one stationary motor vehicle.\n\n| Witness | Where | Light | Lamps | Expected verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| forbid | roadway | night | off | violated |\n| permit | roadway | night | lit | compliant |\n| idle | roadway | day, visibility 5,000 m | off | not applicable |\n| blind | roadway | night | not observed | unknown |\n| branch_1 | shoulder | fog, visibility 120 m | off | violated |\n\n`branch_1` is the only witness that reaches the shoulder and low-visibility branches, so between them the five witnesses cover every branch of the rule.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
